security.evidence:
airsonic-main/src/main/java/org/airsonic/player/service/ConfigurationPropertiesService.java:28-36 - Singleton pattern without synchronization:
private static ConfigurationPropertiesService instance;
public static ConfigurationPropertiesService getInstance() {
    if (instance == null) {
        reset();
    }
    return instance;
}
This unsynchronized singleton can cause race conditions in multithreaded contexts.

airsonic-main/src/main/java/org/airsonic/player/monitor/MetricsManager.java:23-24 - Unsynchronized access to shared static data:
private static volatile Boolean metricsActivatedByConfiguration = null;
private static Object _lock = new Object();
The _lock object is static and mutable but not final, allowing unsynchronized modification.

airsonic-main/src/main/java/org/airsonic/player/service/SettingsService.java:442 - Static mutable cache without proper synchronization:
private static LoadingCache<String, String> transcodeExecutableCache = CacheBuilder.newBuilder()...;
Static shared resource accessed by multiple threads without explicit synchronization beyond the cache's internal mechanisms.

airsonic-main/src/main/java/org/airsonic/player/controller/CoverArtController.java:250-275 - Improper lock release:
try {
    semaphore.acquire();
    ...
} catch (Throwable x) {
    ...
} finally {
    semaphore.release();
}
Semaphore is released in finally block even if acquire() threw an exception, leading to incorrect semaphore count.

airsonic-main/src/main/java/org/airsonic/player/spring/CustomPropertySourceConfigurer.java:18-19 - Static mutable maps used concurrently:
private static final Map<String, Object> DEFAULT_CONSTANTS = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
private static final Map<String, Object> MIGRATED = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
Static mutable collections accessed across multiple threads without additional synchronization beyond ConcurrentHashMap.

airsonic-main/src/main/java/org/airsonic/player/monitor/MetricsManager.java:43-51 - Incorrect synchronization with non-final lock:
private static Object _lock = new Object();
...
if (metricsActivatedByConfiguration == null) {
    synchronized (_lock) {
        if (metricsActivatedByConfiguration == null) {
            configureMetricsActivation();
        }
    }
}
Double-checked locking with non-final lock object can cause synchronization issues if lock is reassigned.
